<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Katanga</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Shaba</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Katanga is a region in the south-east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/democratic-republic-of-the-congo">Democratic Republic of the Congo</a>, rich in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a>, cobalt and uranium. In the 19th century it was dominated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/msiri">Msiri</a>'s Yeke kingdom, and from 1891 it was occupied by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congo-free-state">Congo Free State</a>, later becoming the mining heartland of the Belgian Congo. Its secession under Moise Tshombe in 1960–63 was a central episode of the Congo Crisis, and from 1971 to 1997 it was called Shaba.</p></div>
